WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.167
(cheers and applause)

00:00:18.924 --> 00:00:19.757
- Sit down,

00:00:19.757 --> 00:00:20.842
I know you're excited.

00:00:20.842 --> 00:00:21.844
- Oh my god.

00:00:21.844 --> 00:00:23.045
I love you so much.

00:00:23.045 --> 00:00:23.878
- [Josh] Oh my god,

00:00:23.878 --> 00:00:24.711
I love YOU so much.

00:00:24.711 --> 00:00:25.544
- [Grace] Oh my god, your voice.

00:00:25.544 --> 00:00:26.377
- I was telling you she loves you.

00:00:26.377 --> 00:00:27.440
- So iconic.

00:00:27.440 --> 00:00:28.350
- These are real tears.

00:00:28.350 --> 00:00:30.430
Oh, no!
- She loves you.

00:00:30.430 --> 00:00:31.263
I'm telling you.

00:00:31.263 --> 00:00:32.096
- Oh my god.
- Oh!

00:00:33.442 --> 00:00:36.680
- [Kelly] Can I tell you my favorite part?

00:00:36.680 --> 00:00:38.140
'Cause I was reading her pre-interview,

00:00:38.140 --> 00:00:39.190
and like all the things,

00:00:39.190 --> 00:00:40.660
like, I've seen you in "Book of Mormon",

00:00:40.660 --> 00:00:42.760
I've seen you in "Frozen"
or heard you in "Frozen."

00:00:42.760 --> 00:00:44.120
All the things that you've done.

00:00:44.120 --> 00:00:45.694
Tell him the one you mentioned.

00:00:45.694 --> 00:00:46.527
- Bear claw!

00:00:46.527 --> 00:00:48.025
- [Josh] - [Kelly] Bear claw!

00:00:48.025 --> 00:00:48.858
- Bear claw!

00:00:48.858 --> 00:00:49.960
- Bear claw from "New Girl",

00:00:49.960 --> 00:00:50.805
that's her pull.

00:00:50.805 --> 00:00:54.020
- [Grace] (singing) "Because
you're just a tree!"

00:00:54.020 --> 00:00:55.640
- I also love "Wedding Ringer"!

00:00:55.640 --> 00:00:56.540
- Oh, thank you.

00:00:56.540 --> 00:00:58.210
You're too young to see that, but okay.

00:00:58.210 --> 00:01:00.293
(laughs)

00:01:01.353 --> 00:01:02.186
- [Grace] Shaking.

00:01:02.186 --> 00:01:03.379
- You are so unbelievably talented.

00:01:03.379 --> 00:01:04.212
- Thank you.

00:01:04.212 --> 00:01:05.747
- We were listening to your
song in the car this morning.

00:01:05.747 --> 00:01:06.980
"I Don't Know My Name"

00:01:06.980 --> 00:01:09.135
and I'm blown away by you.

00:01:09.135 --> 00:01:10.502
- Thank you, thank you.
- [Kelly] She's so talented.

00:01:10.502 --> 00:01:11.380
- I'm blown away by you.

00:01:11.380 --> 00:01:12.630
- You are mesmerizing.

00:01:12.630 --> 00:01:13.700
Really incredible.
- Thank you.

00:01:13.700 --> 00:01:14.880
I love that you're crying,

00:01:14.880 --> 00:01:15.713
it's so cool.

00:01:15.713 --> 00:01:16.546
- I'm not crying,

00:01:16.546 --> 00:01:17.379
I'm fine.
- Never lose that though.

00:01:17.379 --> 00:01:18.212
- It was the initial shock.

00:01:18.212 --> 00:01:19.178
It was the initial shock.

00:01:19.178 --> 00:01:20.050
- You shouldn't lose that though.

00:01:20.050 --> 00:01:21.670
I think it's cool when you get so excited

00:01:21.670 --> 00:01:22.503
about meeting people.

00:01:22.503 --> 00:01:23.550
I'm 37 years old and I still,

00:01:23.550 --> 00:01:24.520
ask Meryl Streep.

00:01:24.520 --> 00:01:25.953
I look like an idiot.
(laughs)

00:01:25.953 --> 00:01:27.680
Whatever, I don't care.

00:01:27.680 --> 00:01:28.513
I like her.

00:01:28.513 --> 00:01:29.710
- Mine was Harrison Ford.

00:01:29.710 --> 00:01:31.150
Imagine how that went.

00:01:31.150 --> 00:01:32.520
- Oh my god, was he quiet?

00:01:32.520 --> 00:01:33.705
I feel like he would've been quiet.

00:01:33.705 --> 00:01:34.538
- I literally was like,

00:01:34.538 --> 00:01:35.371
"I love you."

00:01:35.371 --> 00:01:36.338
And he's like, "All right."

00:01:36.338 --> 00:01:39.050
(laughs)

00:01:39.050 --> 00:01:40.270
- So why bear claw?

00:01:40.270 --> 00:01:41.120
Why was that your pull?

00:01:41.120 --> 00:01:42.300
- I love "New Girl".

00:01:42.300 --> 00:01:44.810
I actually just did an
interview with Zooey Deschanel.

00:01:44.810 --> 00:01:45.678
- Oh, I love Zooey.

00:01:45.678 --> 00:01:47.920
- 'Cause I'm like a
diehard "New Girl" fan.

00:01:47.920 --> 00:01:49.500
But they told me on the phone,

00:01:49.500 --> 00:01:50.333
they were like,

00:01:50.333 --> 00:01:53.120
"Okay, so someone's gonna be
sitting with you on the couch."

00:01:53.120 --> 00:01:54.950
And I'm like, "Oh, okay."

00:01:54.950 --> 00:01:55.880
And so,

00:01:55.880 --> 00:01:56.713
they were like,

00:01:56.713 --> 00:01:57.587
"Oh."

00:01:57.587 --> 00:01:58.420
I was like, "Who is it?"

00:01:58.420 --> 00:01:59.253
And they were like, "Josh Gad."

00:01:59.253 --> 00:02:00.086
I was like, "Who's that?"

00:02:00.086 --> 00:02:01.257
So I didn't know who that was.

00:02:01.257 --> 00:02:03.330
But I'm like a huge fan.

00:02:03.330 --> 00:02:04.833
But I know you as Bear Claw.

00:02:06.760 --> 00:02:08.040
- There are so many emotions

00:02:08.040 --> 00:02:09.187
that I'm going through right now.

00:02:09.187 --> 00:02:10.514
(laughs)

00:02:10.514 --> 00:02:11.347
- [Grace] Me too!

00:02:11.347 --> 00:02:12.180
- Didn't know who you were,

00:02:12.180 --> 00:02:14.710
then when I learned who you were, I cried.

00:02:14.710 --> 00:02:16.367
- I cried really hard on the phone.

00:02:16.367 --> 00:02:17.530
- No, I know what you mean though

00:02:17.530 --> 00:02:20.030
'cause I don't ever know
everybody's real name sometimes.

00:02:20.030 --> 00:02:21.030
- Especially actors.

00:02:21.030 --> 00:02:23.210
- I don't know actor's names.
- I'm the same way.

00:02:23.210 --> 00:02:25.120
- Yeah, and I always think
that they're the person

00:02:25.120 --> 00:02:25.953
they were in the movie,

00:02:25.953 --> 00:02:26.786
and they're not.
- [Grace] Oh.

00:02:26.786 --> 00:02:27.878
- Yeah.

00:02:27.878 --> 00:02:28.711
(laughs)

00:02:28.711 --> 00:02:29.544
- We're celebrating Thanksgiving though,

00:02:29.544 --> 00:02:30.620
so what are you thankful for this year?

00:02:30.620 --> 00:02:31.593
- Happy Thanksgiving.

00:02:31.593 --> 00:02:34.790
(cheers and applause)

00:02:34.790 --> 00:02:36.500
- What are you thankful for this year?

00:02:36.500 --> 00:02:38.860
- My family, of course.

00:02:38.860 --> 00:02:39.693
- [Kelly] Yes.

00:02:39.693 --> 00:02:40.620
- I'm very thankful for my family.

00:02:40.620 --> 00:02:41.900
They're very strong.

00:02:41.900 --> 00:02:43.670
- I hear you're making
a special dish, though,

00:02:43.670 --> 00:02:44.503
this Thanksgiving, right?

00:02:44.503 --> 00:02:45.336
- Yes!

00:02:45.336 --> 00:02:46.169
Oh my god.

00:02:46.169 --> 00:02:47.390
Okay, so I just learned,

00:02:47.390 --> 00:02:48.250
well not just,

00:02:48.250 --> 00:02:49.760
I've been learning how to cook

00:02:49.760 --> 00:02:50.760
because I don't know,

00:02:50.760 --> 00:02:52.940
I just really wanted to be like,

00:02:52.940 --> 00:02:54.790
that girl, just like,

00:02:54.790 --> 00:02:56.270
cooking, listening to music,

00:02:56.270 --> 00:02:57.700
like I don't even care,

00:02:57.700 --> 00:02:58.998
messy bun, so.

00:02:58.998 --> 00:03:01.584
- By the way, I love
people who cook like this.

00:03:01.584 --> 00:03:03.930
(laughs)

00:03:03.930 --> 00:03:05.200
- [Kelly] Just get in there, Josh.

00:03:05.200 --> 00:03:06.260
- [Grace] Well, that's
my dream on how to cook.

00:03:06.260 --> 00:03:07.530
So that's the goal.
- Got it.

00:03:07.530 --> 00:03:08.790
- I'm working to get there.

00:03:08.790 --> 00:03:09.623
- Oh.

00:03:09.623 --> 00:03:10.456
- Oh, great!

00:03:10.456 --> 00:03:11.289
Oh, okay!

00:03:11.289 --> 00:03:12.140
- Thank you, Kevin.

00:03:12.140 --> 00:03:13.410
- Thank you very much, Kevin.

00:03:13.410 --> 00:03:14.243
- What's this?

00:03:14.243 --> 00:03:15.140
- Don't look at it!
- I'm not!

00:03:15.140 --> 00:03:15.973
- I'm not done.

00:03:15.973 --> 00:03:17.670
- Totally not.
(laughs)

00:03:17.670 --> 00:03:19.562
- I'm learning how to cook.

00:03:19.562 --> 00:03:21.645
(laughs)

00:03:26.208 --> 00:03:27.041
- Is this mine?

00:03:27.041 --> 00:03:27.874
- I listen.

00:03:27.874 --> 00:03:29.050
- I listen to my guests.

00:03:30.520 --> 00:03:31.661
- That's my water, by the way.

00:03:31.661 --> 00:03:33.744
(laughs)

00:03:36.043 --> 00:03:36.876
It's all right.

00:03:37.915 --> 00:03:39.497
- [Grace] I'm really happy.

00:03:39.497 --> 00:03:42.270
- This is going so well.

00:03:42.270 --> 00:03:43.383
So what is it?

00:03:45.330 --> 00:03:46.200
- Lasagna soup.

00:03:46.200 --> 00:03:47.510
- It's lasagna soup?

00:03:47.510 --> 00:03:48.343
- [Josh] Lasagna soup.

00:03:48.343 --> 00:03:49.760
- I've never heard of lasagna soup.

00:03:49.760 --> 00:03:51.887
- It's lasagna made into a soup.

00:03:51.887 --> 00:03:54.950
- Okay, wait, so can I look at it now?

00:03:54.950 --> 00:03:55.783
- [Grace] Yes.

00:03:55.783 --> 00:03:56.750
- Okay.

00:03:56.750 --> 00:03:58.883
- Did you just play a game of
"Mad Libs" and were like...

00:03:58.883 --> 00:03:59.716
- Yes.

00:04:00.870 --> 00:04:02.290
- So, it's from last night,

00:04:02.290 --> 00:04:04.020
and I don't know how they prepared it.

00:04:04.020 --> 00:04:04.853
- [Kelly] - [Josh] Okay.

00:04:04.853 --> 00:04:06.071
- It used to be in
Ziploc tupperware bowls.

00:04:06.071 --> 00:04:06.904
- They?

00:04:06.904 --> 00:04:09.280
What happened to you in the
kitchen with your dance moves?

00:04:09.280 --> 00:04:10.600
- [Grace] I was in the kitchen.

00:04:10.600 --> 00:04:12.000
- I mean, here's the thing,

00:04:12.000 --> 00:04:12.952
- [Grace] Is it good?

00:04:12.952 --> 00:04:13.785
- Yeah, it's really good, but like...

00:04:13.785 --> 00:04:14.618
- [Grace] Imagine if like-

00:04:14.618 --> 00:04:15.590
- [Kelly] So what makes it soup?

00:04:16.620 --> 00:04:17.453
- Oh!

00:04:18.519 --> 00:04:19.352
A lot of people ask me that.

00:04:19.352 --> 00:04:21.110
- So this is called pasta.

00:04:21.110 --> 00:04:23.633
(laughs)

00:04:23.633 --> 00:04:25.620
- [Grace] Well, no, it's
'cause I do it wrong.

00:04:25.620 --> 00:04:26.453
- I love you!

00:04:27.410 --> 00:04:28.650
- So wait, we did it wrong.

00:04:28.650 --> 00:04:30.530
- I do it incorrectly,

00:04:30.530 --> 00:04:32.320
but that's what now makes it my secret.

00:04:32.320 --> 00:04:33.750
So it's supposed to be soup,

00:04:33.750 --> 00:04:36.090
but I always do it
perfectly every single time,

00:04:36.090 --> 00:04:37.480
and it ends up like that.

00:04:37.480 --> 00:04:39.400
I don't know why.

00:04:39.400 --> 00:04:40.653
- I love you, Grace!

00:04:41.980 --> 00:04:43.670
You're officially my favorite!

00:04:43.670 --> 00:04:45.189
Sorry.

00:04:45.189 --> 00:04:46.540
- Fair enough.

00:04:46.540 --> 00:04:47.990
I've heard a lot of that today.

00:04:47.990 --> 00:04:49.680
- Don't disrespect Josh Gad like that.

00:04:49.680 --> 00:04:50.513
- I'm just kidding.

00:04:50.513 --> 00:04:51.346
- Josh Gad is God.

00:04:51.346 --> 00:04:52.440
- Just kidding.

00:04:52.440 --> 00:04:53.570
You're only 15 though,

00:04:53.570 --> 00:04:55.840
and you just finished
your second EP, right?

00:04:55.840 --> 00:04:57.000
- I released one EP.

00:04:57.000 --> 00:04:58.210
- And this is your second?

00:04:58.210 --> 00:04:59.110
- Volume one.

00:04:59.110 --> 00:04:59.943
- Yeah.

00:04:59.943 --> 00:05:02.410
- So then there will be a volume two.

00:05:02.410 --> 00:05:03.243
- Oh, okay.

00:05:03.243 --> 00:05:05.570
This is "Letters", right?

00:05:05.570 --> 00:05:06.403
- Yes, yes, yes.

00:05:06.403 --> 00:05:08.220
- So wait, I'm excited for you.

00:05:08.220 --> 00:05:09.280
You're actually acting, right?

00:05:09.280 --> 00:05:10.260
In the Disney+ (mumbles).

00:05:10.260 --> 00:05:11.160
- Yeah, yeah, yeah.
- Yeah, "Stargirl".

00:05:11.160 --> 00:05:12.330
What is that about?

00:05:12.330 --> 00:05:14.550
- It's about this girl named Stargirl,

00:05:14.550 --> 00:05:17.500
who was homeschooled and
then goes to a public school.

00:05:17.500 --> 00:05:19.560
- So were you nervous to act?

00:05:19.560 --> 00:05:21.150
I hate acting.

00:05:21.150 --> 00:05:21.983
- You do?

00:05:21.983 --> 00:05:22.933
- Absolutely, 100%.

00:05:22.933 --> 00:05:24.420
- Haven't I seen you in something?

00:05:24.420 --> 00:05:26.483
- Yes.
(laughs)

00:05:27.920 --> 00:05:30.615
We're not talking about one.

00:05:30.615 --> 00:05:31.448
No.

00:05:31.448 --> 00:05:33.689
(cheers and applause)

00:05:33.689 --> 00:05:35.343
Two words.

00:05:35.343 --> 00:05:36.950
Two words, America.

00:05:36.950 --> 00:05:38.750
Contractually obligated.

00:05:38.750 --> 00:05:40.150
I was on that damn show,

00:05:40.150 --> 00:05:42.950
and they made me do that
beach blanket movie.

00:05:42.950 --> 00:05:43.990
I did not want to do it.

00:05:43.990 --> 00:05:44.823
I cried,

00:05:44.823 --> 00:05:45.656
I couldn't get out of it.

00:05:45.656 --> 00:05:47.530
I hate acting.
- Oh, that's the tea.

00:05:47.530 --> 00:05:48.363
- I love actors.

00:05:48.363 --> 00:05:50.410
I think that it's such a gift.

00:05:50.410 --> 00:05:52.020
That's why I freaked out over (crosstalk).

00:05:52.020 --> 00:05:53.910
- They have to be so talented.

00:05:53.910 --> 00:05:57.515
I gained respect and I
lost respect for actors.

00:05:57.515 --> 00:05:59.598
(laughs)

00:06:01.000 --> 00:06:03.302
- You are my favorite guest ever.

00:06:03.302 --> 00:06:05.645
So what is gained and lost?

00:06:05.645 --> 00:06:08.634
- Could I possibly get
a water at some point?

00:06:08.634 --> 00:06:09.467
(laughs)

00:06:09.467 --> 00:06:11.772
- I don't think she drank from this one.

00:06:11.772 --> 00:06:12.772
- I'll wait.

00:06:14.324 --> 00:06:15.670
- I'm (mumbles).
- What did you gain and lose?

00:06:15.670 --> 00:06:16.503
Like, what do you mean?

00:06:16.503 --> 00:06:17.336
- Okay, so it's like,

00:06:17.336 --> 00:06:18.226
okay,

00:06:18.226 --> 00:06:20.290
so it's not as much work as
I thought it was gonna be.

00:06:20.290 --> 00:06:21.680
It's so fun.

00:06:21.680 --> 00:06:23.310
It's really...

00:06:23.310 --> 00:06:24.540
You go to set,

00:06:24.540 --> 00:06:26.570
I don't know if I just
had a weird experience,

00:06:26.570 --> 00:06:27.540
you can tell me,

00:06:27.540 --> 00:06:28.750
but I literally went to set,

00:06:28.750 --> 00:06:30.660
there was just tons of catering,

00:06:30.660 --> 00:06:31.690
read your lines,

00:06:31.690 --> 00:06:33.900
and hang out with the cast.

00:06:33.900 --> 00:06:35.130
- You had a weird experience.

00:06:35.130 --> 00:06:37.913
(laughs)

00:06:37.913 --> 00:06:39.210
- I had a special experience.

00:06:39.210 --> 00:06:43.000
- I'm fascinated by how
advanced you are for your age.

00:06:43.000 --> 00:06:43.833
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:06:43.833 --> 00:06:45.720
- Like, how are you so mature?

00:06:45.720 --> 00:06:46.636
- I can't believe I'm
talking to you right now.

00:06:46.636 --> 00:06:49.932
(laughs)
It's so incredible.

00:06:49.932 --> 00:06:50.765
- Five minutes ago,

00:06:50.765 --> 00:06:52.550
you didn't know who I was and were crying.

00:06:54.950 --> 00:06:55.783
- I don't know.

00:06:55.783 --> 00:06:56.680
I'm the youngest.

00:06:56.680 --> 00:06:57.750
- Were you always,

00:06:57.750 --> 00:06:58.770
how many siblings do you have?

00:06:58.770 --> 00:06:59.880
- I have two siblings.

00:06:59.880 --> 00:07:01.160
And my one sister is 18,

00:07:01.160 --> 00:07:02.910
and my other brother is 20,

00:07:02.910 --> 00:07:05.010
so I have always been like this

00:07:05.010 --> 00:07:07.040
'cause I kind of followed their age gap.

00:07:07.040 --> 00:07:07.880
- We have kids.

00:07:07.880 --> 00:07:09.460
Some of your kids are
a little more advanced

00:07:09.460 --> 00:07:10.660
than the others.
(laughs)

00:07:10.660 --> 00:07:13.590
- None of my kids talk this way.

00:07:13.590 --> 00:07:15.597
I'm gonna make them watch
this interview and be like,

00:07:15.597 --> 00:07:16.597
"Do that."

